# Meeting Summary - Platform Decision: Azure + Microsoft Fabric

**Date:** 2026-08-31
**Participants:** Person A (Chief Data Officer, MNC Pvt Ltd; Client Sponsor); Person B (Head of BI & Reporting, MNC Pvt Ltd); Person C (Head of IT Infrastructure, MNC Pvt Ltd); Person D (Enterprise Architect, Delivery Team); Person E (Platform Engineering Lead, Delivery Team)
**Purpose:** Decide between Microsoft Fabric and Azure Databricks as the analytics compute engine within the previously selected Azure cloud direction, and identify dependencies and next steps for platform setup.

## Executive summary
The group evaluated Microsoft Fabric and Azure Databricks against team skill fit, time to first value, cost predictability, existing tool investment reuse, governance and semantic-layer fit, and operational overhead. The group agreed to proceed with Azure and Microsoft Fabric because it better fits the existing GUI-driven and Power BI-oriented environment, supports a shorter path to the Supply Chain use case, offers more predictable capacity-based pricing, and reduces operational overhead. The decision is scoped to current reporting-and-analytics-first requirements and may be revisited if heavy machine-learning or data-science needs grow materially. ADLS Gen2 remains the storage foundation, while Fabric capacity sizing, Entra ID integration, semantic-layer redesign, parallel running, and team enablement are dependencies. Person D will formalize the decision in an ADR and circulate it for Person A's sign-off before it is treated as final.

